WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.125 --> 00:00:02.915
(uplifting orchestral music)

00:00:02.915 --> 00:00:06.837
- Ralph Waldo Emerson once quoted that,

00:00:06.837 --> 00:00:11.575
"Nothing great can ever be
achieved without enthusiasm."

00:00:11.575 --> 00:00:14.158
Might have a lot of enthusiasm.

00:00:20.271 --> 00:00:23.317
This is Northlandz in
Flemington, New Jersey.

00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:27.400
Northlandz is the world's
largest model railroad.

00:00:28.608 --> 00:00:31.551
Well, I guess, you know, everybody has
a passion for something.

00:00:31.551 --> 00:00:32.427
My thing was trains.

00:00:32.427 --> 00:00:35.051
I had trains around the
Christmas tree as a kid.

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:37.491
Wherever I lived, I'm
planning track plans,

00:00:37.491 --> 00:00:39.902
and then over 18 years
I added five basements

00:00:39.902 --> 00:00:41.353
onto the house.

00:00:41.353 --> 00:00:43.683
And from that I got fairly
good at making mountains,

00:00:43.683 --> 00:00:45.630
and bridges, and design work.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.163
And we decided to give it to the world,

00:00:47.163 --> 00:00:48.591
so we tore it all down,

00:00:48.591 --> 00:00:50.971
bought this land, built Northlandz.

00:00:50.971 --> 00:00:54.821
Any given day we run
between 85 and 90 trains.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.113
Some of the details in Northlandz inside,

00:00:57.113 --> 00:00:58.993
about 40,000 feet of track,

00:00:58.993 --> 00:01:00.971
'bout 4,000 buildings,

00:01:00.971 --> 00:01:02.673
over 400 bridges.

00:01:02.673 --> 00:01:06.433
Many of the mountains in
here are 3 1/2 stories high.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.433
Most things in here are scratch built.

00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:10.846
Underneath the entire super
structure there's enough lumber

00:01:10.846 --> 00:01:13.851
to build about 42 large houses.

00:01:13.851 --> 00:01:15.262
Takes a few hours to go through

00:01:15.262 --> 00:01:19.043
for the average person to see everything.

00:01:19.043 --> 00:01:22.523
We went millions into
debt to build this place.

00:01:22.523 --> 00:01:24.043
Everybody thought we were nuts.

00:01:24.043 --> 00:01:25.111
And the only one that believed

00:01:25.111 --> 00:01:27.102
in what I wanted to do was my wife,

00:01:27.102 --> 00:01:30.662
and she was totally with
me on this big time.

00:01:30.662 --> 00:01:32.563
It's an artistic endeavor.

00:01:32.563 --> 00:01:35.062
It's a gift to the world of what I can do,

00:01:35.062 --> 00:01:37.979
and it makes a lot of people happy.

